WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.287
In normal application code, we rarely rebuild every encoder layer by hand.

00:00:05.287 --> 00:00:12.147
PyTorch provides TransformerEncoderLayer, which bundles self-attention, feed-forward processing,

00:00:12.147 --> 00:00:17.927
residual connections, normalization, and dropout into a reusable component.

00:00:17.927 --> 00:00:23.592
The code lets us specify d_model, the hidden size, and nhead, the number of attention heads.

00:00:23.592 --> 00:00:29.267
Passing a tensor through the layer returns another tensor with the same sequence structure and hidden

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:37.067
dimension. Use this built-in layer to confirm the architecture we constructed manually.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:42.022
The manual version is valuable because it teaches what the components do.

00:00:42.022 --> 00:00:47.272
The built-in version is valuable because it reduces implementation mistakes.

00:00:47.272 --> 00:00:54.742
In pretrained NLP work, we usually go one step further and load an entire architecture through Hugging Face

00:00:54.742 --> 00:00:57.487
rather than assembling the blocks ourselves.

00:00:57.487 --> 00:01:04.636
Still, knowing what TransformerEncoderLayer contains makes pretrained models much less of a black box.
